//github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T17:10:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T17:10:28Z","body":"For posterity I want to explain why the fact that memcpy() with either dest or src is undefined behavior matters:\r\n\r\nWe trigger the following sequence of events:\r\n\r\n1) memcpy(null, null, 0) is UB, thus dest and src cannot be null\r\n2) we inline the calls to the ctor and dtor\r\n3) now we have a function that does something that \"proves\" dest cannot be null\r\n4) we inline cowdata::_unref() which does a null check, on something that the compiler just convinced itself cannot be null\r\n5) the compiler removes the dead code branch where _ptr == nullptr\r\n6) we start to do pointer arithmetic on a nullptr and get send to uninitialized memory.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2546184474/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2549906153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100422#issuecomment-2549906153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100422","id":2549906153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X_Hrp","user":{"lo